{"name":"Space Opera","hex":"#5511dd","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"space opera","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A subgenre of speculative fiction or science fiction that emphasizes space travel, romantic adventure, and larger-than-life characters often set against vast exotic settings.","A subgenre of speculative fiction or science fiction that uses serialization."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/space_opera"}],"entries":[{"title":"Space opera","blocks":[{"text":"Space opera is a subgenre of science fiction and science fantasy that emphasizes epic outer space adventures set in a universe in which faster-than-light travel has become common. The plots often play out against a backdrop of space warfare, alien civilizations and galactic empires. The sub-genre is sometimes thought of as a futuristic homage to earlier adventure sagas, such as those found in mythology and chivalric romance."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Imagination_195606.jpg/330px-Imagination_195606.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space_opera"},{"title":"Space Opera (role-playing game)","blocks":[{"text":"Space Opera is a science-fiction role-playing game created by Edward E. Simbalist, A. Mark Ratner, and Phil McGregor in 1980 for Fantasy Games Unlimited (FGU). While the game's system can be used to create any science fiction genre, Space Opera has a default setting focused on creating space opera themed adventures."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3a/Spaceoperacover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space_Opera_(role-playing_game)"},{"title":"Space","blocks":[{"text":"Space is a three-dimensional continuum containing positions and directions. In classical physics, physical space is often conceived in three linear dimensions. Modern physicists usually consider it, with time, to be part of a boundless four-dimensional continuum known as spacetime. The concept of space is considered to be of fundamental importance to an understanding of the physical universe. However, disagreement continues between philosophers over whether it is itself an entity, a relationship between entities, or part of a conceptual framework."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/3D_coordinate_system.svg/330px-3D_coordinate_system.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space"},{"title":"Opera","blocks":[{"text":"Opera is a form of Western theatre in which music is a fundamental component and dramatic roles are taken by singers. Such a \"work\" is typically a collaboration between a composer and a librettist and incorporates a number of the performing arts, such as acting, scenery, costume, and sometimes dance or ballet. The performance is typically given in an opera house, accompanied by an orchestra or smaller musical ensemble, which since the early 19th century has been led by a conductor. Although musical theatre is closely related to opera, the two are considered to be distinct from one another."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Macbeth_applause_at_Savonlinna_Opera_festival_in_2007_-_panoramio.jpg/330px-Macbeth_applause_at_Savonlinna_Opera_festival_in_2007_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opera"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/GalaxyOct50rearcover.jpg/500px-GalaxyOct50rearcover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/GalaxyOct50rearcover.jpg/500px-GalaxyOct50rearcover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail